From: Alan Shearer
Subject: virtio_gpu: delete framebuffer and shared areas in free()

open() creates the framebuffer and shared-info areas. close() only
stops the update thread and deletes commandDone. free() waits for
the thread and frees the handle, but never deletes those areas.
uninit_device() only deletes the command area.

Delete both areas in free() after the update thread has exited and
completed virtqueue entries have been drained.

The driver still uses one set of areas on the device cookie. A
second open() is not refcounted; that is pre-existing and not
fixed here.

---
 src/add-ons/kernel/drivers/graphics/virtio/virtio_gpu.cpp | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/add-ons/kernel/drivers/graphics/virtio/virtio_gpu.cpp b/src/add-ons/kernel/drivers/graphics/virtio/virtio_gpu.cpp
--- a/src/add-ons/kernel/drivers/graphics/virtio/virtio_gpu.cpp
+++ b/src/add-ons/kernel/drivers/graphics/virtio/virtio_gpu.cpp
@@ -675,6 +675,10 @@ virtio_gpu_free(void* cookie)
 	wait_for_thread(info->updateThread, &result);
 	info->updateThread = -1;
 	virtio_gpu_drain_queues(info);
+	delete_area(info->framebufferArea);
+	info->framebufferArea = -1;
+	delete_area(info->sharedArea);
+	info->sharedArea = -1;
 	free(handle);
 	return B_OK;
 }
